_L06_R_Q22</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Which revision best changes &amp;quot;I was scared&amp;quot; into mood and tension?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;I was very scared.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Fear happened.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Scared scared scared.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The floorboard creaked behind me, and I stopped breathing long enough to hear it creak again.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U02_L06_R_Q23</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Which choice best identifies tone in this sentence? &amp;quot;Naturally, the one day I needed the printer, it decided to become a decorative sculpture.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Solemn and ceremonial&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Neutral and scientific&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Sarcastic or humorous&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Terrified&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U02_L06_R_Q24</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;What should a writer do when a scene feels flat?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Add unrelated events.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Remove all sensory detail.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Keep the flat version unchanged.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Decide the intended effect, then revise pace, detail, diction, imagery, or sentence length to create it.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U02_L06_R_Q25</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Which checkpoint explanation meets mastery?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;I slowed the moment when the phone lit up by adding two actions and a reflection in the screen. This creates tension because the reader waits to see whether the narrator will answer.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;I made it tense because it is tense.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;I wrote a scene.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;I used a character name.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question></quiz>